# Mule Global Configuration Standards

## All Global Config in One File
- All global configuration elements **must** be defined in `src/main/mule/common/global-config.xml` (or `global.xml`)
- This includes HTTP listeners, ObjectStore references, connector configs, APIKit config, error handler refs, etc.
- **No configuration elements** should exist in implementation flow files

## Configuration Element Naming
- Format: `{description}_{type}` with description parts separated by hyphens
- Examples:
  - `customer-sapi_httpListenerConfig`
  - `env_propertiesConfig`
  - `oauth_objectStore`
- Exception: Global Property elements use the variable name (e.g., `mule.env`)
- Library-defined elements are prefixed with the library name (e.g., `common-selfsigned_tlsContext`)
- When both `name` and `doc:name` exist, set them to the **same value**

## No Hard-Coded Values
- All values that change per environment **must** be parameterized via properties:
  - HTTP listener host, port, protocol
  - API autodiscovery ID and base path
  - Environment name and encryption key
  - Backend connector host/port
  - Retry counts and timeout settings
- Flag any literal host, port, URL, or credential in configuration elements

## Review Checklist
- [ ] No global config elements defined outside the global config file
- [ ] Config element names follow `{description}_{type}` format
- [ ] No hard-coded hosts, ports, URLs, or credentials in config elements
- [ ] Properties are used for all environment-specific values
